@startuml Unified Primary Workflow - Project A
!theme blueprint
title Project A - Unified Document Processing Pipeline
caption Consolidated from Planning Docs + Copilot + Gemini + Sonnet analyses (Opus synthesis)

skinparam BackgroundColor transparent
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #2C3E50
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

' Color coding for different stages
skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor<<Input>> #E8F5E9
    BackgroundColor<<Preflight>> #FFF3E0
    BackgroundColor<<Gate>> #E3F2FD
    BackgroundColor<<Detection>> #F3E5F5
    BackgroundColor<<ML>> #FCE4EC
    BackgroundColor<<Correction>> #FFF9C4
    BackgroundColor<<Quality>> #E0F2F1
    BackgroundColor<<Output>> #F1F8E9
    BackgroundColor<<Error>> #FFEBEE
    BorderColor #2C3E50
}

|#E8F5E9|Initialization|
start
:Load Configuration<<Input>>;
note right
  **Module:** core/config.py
  **Source:** YAML + Environment

  **Key Settings:**
  - enable_pdf_upscaling
  - teacher_fallback_enabled
  - entropy_threshold: 0.8
  - discrepancy_threshold: 0.3
end note

:Initialize Components<<Input>>;
note right
  **Components:**
  - DocumentProcessor
  - PDFDocumentAnalyzer
  - TextGate
  - ClassicalIQADetector (7 detectors)
  - MLIQADetector (ONNX Runtime)
  - LayoutLiteAnalyzer
  - CorrectionPipeline
  - DQSCalculator
  - RoutingEngine
end note

|#FFF3E0|Pre-flight|
:Input Document (PDF/Image)<<Input>>;
note right
  **Supported:**
  PDF, PNG, JPEG, TIFF

  **Validation:**
  - File existence
  - MIME type detection
  - Size limits
end note

partition "DPI Analysis & Upscaling (Phase 4)" {
  :PDFResolutionAnalyzer.analyze()<<Preflight>>;
  note right
    **Module:** ingestion/pdf_resolution.py

    **Process:**
    1. Extract image dimensions
    2. Calculate effective DPI
    3. Return resolution metrics

    **Output:** min_dpi, avg_dpi, needs_upscaling
    **Time:** <100ms
  end note

  if (DPI < 300?) then (yes)
    if (Upscaling Enabled?) then (yes)
      :PDFUpscaler.upscale()<<Preflight>>;
      note right
        **Module:** ingestion/pdf_upscaler.py

        **Algorithms:**
        - LANCZOS (default, best quality)
        - BICUBIC (balanced)
        - INTER_LINEAR (fastest)

        **Time:** 310-360ms/page
        **Memory:** <2GB
      end note

      if (Success?) then (yes)
        :Use Upscaled Document;
      else (no)
        if (Preserve Original?) then (yes)
          :Fallback to Original<<Error>>;
        else (no)
          :Raise Error<<Error>>;
          stop
        endif
      endif
    else (no)
      :Skip (Config Disabled);
    endif
  else (no)
    :Skip (DPI Sufficient);
  endif
}

|#E3F2FD|Ingestion|
partition "Document Loading" {
  if (PDF?) then (yes)
    :PDFLoader.load_pages()<<Input>>;
    note right
      **Module:** ingestion/pdf_loader.py
      **Library:** PyMuPDF (fitz)

      **Process:**
      1. Open PDF
      2. Render pages at 300 DPI
      3. Convert to numpy (BGR)

      **Output:** List[PageImage]
    end note
  else (Image)
    :ImageLoader.load()<<Input>>;
    note right
      **Module:** ingestion/image_loader.py
      **Library:** Pillow

      **Handles:** PNG, JPEG, TIFF
      **Extracts:** EXIF DPI
    end note
  endif

  :Normalize to 300 DPI<<Input>>;
  note right
    - Standardize color space (BGR)
    - COCO coordinate format
    - Generate document_id
  end note
}

|#E3F2FD|Classification|
partition "PDF Type Classification (Phase 8)" {
  :PDFTypeClassifier.classify()<<Gate>>;
  note right
    **Module:** classification/pdf_type_classifier.py

    **Method:** PyMuPDF text extraction ratio

    **Logic:**
    - text_ratio > 0.8 → BORN_DIGITAL
    - text_ratio < 0.2 → IMAGE_ONLY
    - else → HYBRID

    **Accuracy:** >99%
  end note
}

partition "Text Gate Routing" {
  :TextGate.detect()<<Gate>>;
  note right
    **Module:** detection/text_gate.py

    **Ensemble Heuristics:**
    1. Morphological stroke density (weight: 0.4)
    2. Connected components (weight: 0.4)
    3. Canny edge density (weight: 0.2)

    **Threshold:** stroke_density > 0.05 OR components > 10
    **Time:** <10ms (target <50ms)
  end note
}

|#F3E5F5|Detection|
fork
  if (has_text?) then (no)
    |#F3E5F5|No Text Path|
    partition "Classical IQA (Full Page)" {
      :Run 7 Classical Detectors<<Detection>>;
      note right
        **Module:** detection/iqa_classical.py

        **Phase 1 (Basic):**
        1. BlurDetector (Laplacian variance)
        2. SkewDetector (Hough + projection)
        3. ContrastDetector (histogram)

        **Phase 1C (Enhanced):**
        4. NoiseDetector (wavelet DWT)
        5. IlluminationDetector (9-region)
        6. JPEGBlockinessDetector (DCT)
        7. BleedThroughDetector (verso)

        **Total Time:** <25ms (all 7)
      end note

      :ClassicalScoreAdapter.normalize()<<Detection>>;
      note right
        Convert all outputs to [0, 1] range
        for consistent comparison
      end note
    }
  else (yes)
    |#F3E5F5|Text Path|
    partition "Layout-Lite Detection (Phase 6)" {
      :DocLayout-YOLO Inference<<Detection>>;
      note right
        **Module:** detection/layout_lite/analyzer.py
        **Model:** DocLayout-YOLO (ONNX)
        **Config:** configs/models/doclayout_yolo.yaml

        **11 DocLayNet Classes:**
        Caption, Footnote, Formula, List-Item,
        Page-Footer, Page-Header, Picture,
        Section-Header, Table, Text, Title

        **Time:** <30ms GPU, <100ms CPU
      end note

      :Extract Page Attributes<<Detection>>;
      note right
        **Coarse Classification:**
        - layout_type: single/multi/complex
        - has_tables: bool
        - has_figures: bool
        - has_dense_math: bool
        - has_handwriting: bool

        **NOT Semantic Layout:**
        - No reading order
        - No table structure
        - No element linking
        (Project B responsibility)
      end note

      :Calculate Complexity Score<<Detection>>;
      note right
        **Formula:**
        score = base[layout_type]
              + 0.20 * has_tables
              + 0.15 * has_figures
              + 0.15 * has_dense_math
              + 0.10 * has_handwriting

        **Range:** [0, 1]
      end note
    }
  endif

fork again
  |#FCE4EC|ML IQA|
  partition "Student ML IQA (Primary)" {
    :MLIQADetector.run_student()<<ML>>;
    note right
      **Module:** detection/iqa_ml.py
      **Model:** ResNet-18 Student (ONNX)
      **Size:** 42 MB (12.3M params)

      **Device Priority:**
      1. Local GPU (CUDA)
      2. Local CPU (ONNX)

      **Time:** <10ms GPU, <40ms CPU
    end note

    :Preprocess (224x224)<<ML>>;
    note right
      1. Resize to 224x224
      2. BGR → RGB
      3. Normalize [0,1]
      4. ImageNet standardization
      5. HWC → CHW
    end note

    :5-Head Classification<<ML>>;
    note right
      **Heads:**
      - blur_score
      - noise_score
      - contrast_score
      - skew_score
      - compression_score

      **Each:** Binary classification + confidence
    end note

    :Calculate Uncertainty<<ML>>;
    note right
      **UncertaintyMetrics:**
      - entropy = -Σ p(i) * log2(p(i))
      - min_confidence
      - mean_confidence
    end note
  }

  partition "Teacher Escalation Gate" {
    :Check Escalation Triggers<<ML>>;
    note right
      **6 Trigger Conditions:**

      **1. High Uncertainty:**
      - entropy >= 0.8
      - min_confidence < 0.6
      - mean_confidence < 0.7

      **2. Classical Discrepancy:**
      - |student - classical| >= 0.3

      **3. High-Risk Document:**
      - pre_ocr_risk >= 0.6
      - pdf_type == IMAGE_ONLY
      - complexity_score > 0.6

      **4. Config Override:**
      - force_teacher_inference: true

      **5. Budget Check (BLOCKING):**
      - max_pages_for_teacher exceeded
      - Modal budget exceeded

      **6. Device Check (BLOCKING):**
      - No GPU available (local or Modal)
    end note

    if (Should Escalate?) then (yes)
      if (GPU Available?) then (yes)
        partition "Teacher ML IQA (Selective)" {
          :MLIQADetector.run_teacher()<<ML>>;
          note right
            **Model:** ResNet-50 Teacher (ONNX)
            **Size:** 105 MB (30.5M params)

            **Device Priority:**
            1. Local GPU
            2. Modal GPU (if budget OK)
            3. BLOCK (no CPU teacher)

            **Time:** <30ms GPU
            **Target:** <10% pages escalated
          end note

          :Merge Results (Teacher Override)<<ML>>;
          note right
            **Strategy:** Use teacher scores,
            discard student for this page

            **Log:**
            - page_numbers
            - escalation_reason
            - inference_time_ms
          end note
        }
      else (no)
        :Fallback to Student<<ML>>;
        note right
          Graceful degradation:
          - Log warning
          - Use student results
          - Flag in metadata
        end note
      endif
    else (no)
      :Use Student Results<<ML>>;
    endif
  }
endfork

:Merge All IQA Results<<ML>>;
note right
  **Final Scores:**
  - Source: student OR teacher
  - 5 quality dimensions
  - Confidence metrics
  - Classical comparison
end note

|#FFF9C4|Correction|
partition "Apply Corrections (Phase 5)" {
  if (is_skewed AND angle > 0.5°?) then (yes)
    :DeskewCorrector.apply()<<Correction>>;
    note right
      **Guardrails:**
      - Skip if angle > 45°
      - Skip if confidence < 0.3
      - Track transform history
    end note
  endif

  if (low_contrast?) then (yes)
    :ContrastEnhancer.apply()<<Correction>>;
    note right
      **CLAHE:**
      - clipLimit: 2.0
      - tileGridSize: (8, 8)
    end note
  endif

  if (is_blurry?) then (yes)
    :Sharpener.apply()<<Correction>>;
    note right
      **Unsharp Mask:**
      Severity-based adjustment
    end note
  endif

  if (has_noise?) then (yes)
    :Denoiser.apply()<<Correction>>;
    note right
      **OpenCV fastNlMeans:**
      - h: 10
      - Skip if blur_score < 0.3
    end note
  endif

  :Quality Re-verification<<Correction>>;
  note right
    **Before/After Comparison:**
    - Re-run Classical IQA
    - Rollback if degraded
    - Track in transform_history
  end note
}

|#E0F2F1|Quality Scoring|
partition "DQS Calculation (Phase 8)" {
  :Calculate Degradation Score<<Quality>>;
  note right
    **Module:** metrics/dqs_calculator.py

    **Weights:**
    - blur: 0.30
    - noise: 0.25
    - contrast: 0.20
    - illumination: 0.15
    - artifacts: 0.10

    **ML Blend:** 0.30 (30% ML + 70% classical)
  end note

  :Calculate Structural Complexity<<Quality>>;
  note right
    **Base Scores:**
    - SINGLE_COLUMN: 0.1
    - MULTI_COLUMN: 0.4
    - THREE_COLUMN: 0.6
    - COMPLEX: 0.9

    **+ Feature weights**
  end note

  :Calculate Pre-OCR Risk<<Quality>>;
  note right
    **Formula:**
    risk = 0.40 * degradation
         + 0.30 * complexity
         + 0.20 * (pdf_type == IMAGE_ONLY)
         + 0.10 * has_handwriting

    **Range:** [0, 1]
    - 0.0-0.3: Low risk
    - 0.3-0.6: Medium risk
    - 0.6-1.0: High risk
  end note
}

partition "Routing Recommendation (Phase 8)" {
  :RoutingEngine.recommend()<<Quality>>;
  note right
    **Module:** routing/recommendation_engine.py

    **Decision Tree (5 Rules):**

    **Rule 1:** has_tables OR has_figures
    → VISION_STRUCTURED

    **Rule 2:** risk > 0.6 OR has_handwriting
    → OCR_ADVANCED

    **Rule 3:** BORN_DIGITAL + quality > 0.8 + simple
    → OCR_FAST

    **Rule 4:** IMAGE_ONLY + simple
    → VISION_SIMPLE

    **Rule 5:** Fallback
    → OCR_ADVANCED
  end note

  :Generate Rationale<<Quality>>;
}

|#F1F8E9|Output|
partition "DocumentMetadata Assembly" {
  :Create DocumentMetadata<<Output>>;
  note right
    **Module:** schema.py (Pydantic v2)

    **Fields:**
    - document_id, file_name
    - pdf_type: PDFType
    - num_pages: int
    - pre_ocr_risk: float
    - dqs: DQSMetadata
    - ocr_routing_recommendation
    - page_layout_summary: list
    - upscaling: UpscalingMetadata
    - teacher_usage: TeacherUsageMetadata
    - processing_version
    - pages: list[PageMetadata]
  end note

  :Serialize to JSON<<Output>>;
  note right
    **Output:** DocumentMetadata.json
    - Pretty printed (indent=2)
    - UTF-8 encoding
    - COCO-aligned bboxes
    - ISO 8601 timestamps
  end note
}

partition "Image Output" {
  :Write Corrected Images<<Output>>;
  note right
    **Format:**
    {document_id}_page_{idx:04d}.png

    **Quality:**
    - 300 DPI
    - Lossless PNG
    - RGB color space
  end note
}

:Package for Project B Handoff<<Output>>;
note right
  **Deliverables:**
  1. DocumentMetadata.json
  2. Corrected page images
  3. Processing logs

  **Project B receives:**
  - OCR strategy guidance
  - Pre-assessed quality
  - Structural metadata
end note

stop

legend right
  **Performance Summary:**
  |= Stage |= GPU |= CPU |
  | Pre-flight | <100ms | <100ms |
  | DPI Upscaling | 310-360ms | 310-360ms |
  | Text Gate | <10ms | <10ms |
  | Classical IQA | <25ms | <25ms |
  | Student ML IQA | <10ms | <40ms |
  | Teacher ML IQA | <30ms | N/A |
  | Layout-Lite | <30ms | <100ms |
  | Corrections | <100ms | <100ms |
  | **Total** | **<150ms** | **<500ms** |

  **Quality Targets:**
  - IQA mAP: >0.88
  - Routing accuracy: >90%
  - Teacher escalation: <10%
  - Coverage: >80%

  **Key Modules:**
  - ingestion/ - PDF/image loading
  - detection/ - IQA + layout
  - correction/ - Image transforms
  - metrics/ - DQS calculation
  - routing/ - Recommendation engine
  - output/ - JSON + image export

  **Synthesized from:**
  - Planning docs (official)
  - Copilot (artifact promotion)
  - Sonnet (comprehensive detail)
  - ADR-029 (scope boundaries)

  **Excluded:**
  - Per-element Hybrid IQA (ADR-029: deferred)
  - Gemini per-element approach
endlegend

@enduml
